      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1158",
      "html": "<ul><li><strong>Scientific name:</strong> Otocinclus huaorani Schaefer, 1997</li><li><strong>Common names:</strong> Ecuador Oto, Huarani Otocinclus</li><li><strong>Size:</strong> 32 mm (1.3\") SL</li><li><strong>Temperature:</strong> 26.0–30.0°C (78.8–86°F)</li><li><strong>IUCN Red List:</strong> Least Concern (last assessed 2014)</li><li><strong>Etymology:</strong> Greek ous, oto = ear + Latin cinclus = latticework, in allusion to the holes of the head in the ears. The specific epithet is based on the Huaorani people who are native to the Upper Napo River area in Ecuador.</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1158",
      "html": "<p>South America: western upper Amazon and Orinoco River basins. Type locality: tributary to Río San Miguel (kilometer 50, 4.5 kilometers south of Tipischca), about 0°10'N, 76°13'W, Río Amazonas/Napo basin, Napo, Ecuador.</p>"
    },
    {
